{
    "article_summary": "This article describes the integration of nitrilase (NIT) enzymes with photoredox catalysis to convert organonitriles into fluorinated, trifluoromethylated, and pentafluoroethylated products. The process involves a one-pot chemoenzymatic cascade where nitriles are first hydrolyzed to carboxylic acids by bacterial nitrilases (as cell-free lysates), followed by a photoredox-catalyzed decarboxylative functionalization using reagents like Selectfluor, Togni's reagent, or a hypervalent iodine pentafluoroethylating agent.",
